From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:19:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] BGP: Fix crash on start with interface range

Triggered by any BGP protocol using `interface range`, e.g.
`protocol bgp { ...; interface range "eth*"; strict bind; ... }`: bird
segfaults on startup, or on configure adding such a protocol.

Since commit 21637833e ("BGP: Block connections on explicitly disabled
instances") bgp_init() registers the default listen request right away.
bgp_default_listen_request() returns NULL for interface patterns, as
their requests come from the interface notifier, and
bgp_listen_register() dereferences it.

Register the default request only if there is one.

Fixes: 21637833e ("BGP: Block connections on explicitly disabled instances")
---
--- a/proto/bgp/bgp.c
+++ b/proto/bgp/bgp.c
@@ -3150,8 +3150,11 @@ bgp_init(struct proto_config *CF)
   init_list(&p->listen);
 
   /* Create listener request immediately to capture and block
-   * incoming connections if disabled */
-  bgp_listen_register(p, bgp_default_listen_request(p));
+   * incoming connections if disabled. There is none for interface
+   * patterns, these get their requests from the interface notifier. */
+  struct bgp_listen_request *req = bgp_default_listen_request(p);
+  if (req)
+    bgp_listen_register(p, req);
 
   /* Hack: We use cf->remote_ip just to pass remote_ip from bgp_spawn() */
   if (cf->c.parent)
